            <ArticleTitle>Three cases of acute myocardial infarction due to coronary embolism: treatment using a thrombus aspiration device.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>861-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this report, we describe three patients with acute myocardial infarction due to coronary embolism who were successfully treated using a thrombus aspiration device. Thrombus aspiration is shown to be a feasible and effective strategy for the treatment of acute coronary embolism.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
